To qualify for the protection under California’s lemon law, your vehicle must meet the following criteria:

- The manufacturer has made multiple unsuccessful attempts to fix the warranty-covered defect.

- Your vehicle has been out of service for warranty repairs for 30 or more total days.

- The defect was not a result of driver abuse, neglect, or error.

